2:[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://dottodotfreeprintables.com/fr/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Playgrounds\",\"item\":\"https://dottodotfreeprintables.com/fr/playgrounds/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Aire de jeux de montagnes russes\",\"item\":\"https://dottodotfreeprintables.com/fr/playgrounds/slide-playgrounds-dot-to-dot-puzzle/\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"CreativeWork\",\"name\":\"Aire de jeux de montagnes russes\",\"description\":\"Prêt pour 102 points ? Grimpez et descendez un grand toboggan de terrain de jeu dans ce défi PDF imprimable détaillé pour les compteurs confiants de 6 à 10 ans.\",\"educationalUse\":\"Fine motor skills, number sequencing\"}"}}],["$","main",null,{"children":[["$","nav",null,{"className":"breadcrumb","aria-label":"Fil d'Ariane","children":[["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/fr/","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":14,"height":14,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-house","aria-hidden":"true","children":[["$","path","5wwlr5",{"d":"M15 21v-8a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v8"}],["$","path","1d0kgt",{"d":"M3 10a2 2 0 0 1 .709-1.528l7-5.999a2 2 0 0 1 2.582 0l7 5.999A2 2 0 0 1 21 10v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"}],"$undefined"]}]," ","Maison"]}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":" › "}],["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/fr/playgrounds/","children":"Playgrounds"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":" › "}],["$","span",null,{"aria-current":"page","children":"Aire de jeux de montagnes russes"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"maxWidth":1180,"margin":"0 auto","padding":"0 24px 20px"},"children":null}],["$","div",null,{"className":"puzzle-page-layout section","style":{"paddingTop":0},"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"puzzle-preview-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"puzzle-preview-card","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"","srcSet":"$undefined","sizes":"$undefined","alt":"Piste de montagnes russes en boucle serpentant à travers 133 points à relier, notre fiche la plus extrême","width":540,"height":420,"loading":"eager","fetchPriority":"high","decoding":"async","className":"$undefined","style":{"width":"100%","height":"auto","display":"block","borderRadius":16}}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"puzzle-side-ad","children":null}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"puzzle-details-col","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":["Free ","Playgrounds"," Printable"]}],["$","h1",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem)"},"children":"Aire de jeux de montagnes russes Dot-to-Dot Printable"}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"color":"var(--muted)","fontSize":"1.05rem","lineHeight":1.65,"margin":"14px 0 20px"},"children":"Relie 133 points pour révéler un circuit de montagnes russes complet, avec tous ses loopings. C'est notre puzzle le plus difficile à ce jour, conçu pour les enfants qui ont déjà terminé les modèles plus faciles et qui recherchent un véritable défi de patience et de précision."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"meta-chips","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"chip","children":["Ages:"," ",""]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"chip","children":["Dots:"," 1–",0]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"chip chip--free","children":"100% Free"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"margin":"16px 0"},"children":[["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":8,"fontSize":"0.9rem"},"children":"Difficulty"}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","alignItems":"center","gap":10},"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"difficulty","role":"img","aria-label":"Niveau de difficulté 1 sur 3","style":{"margin":0},"children":[["$","span","1",{"className":"on"}],["$","span","2",{"className":""}],["$","span","3",{"className":""}]]}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"0.85rem","fontWeight":800,"color":"var(--muted)"},"children":"Easy"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"fun-fact-box","children":[["$","span",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1.3rem"},"aria-hidden":"true","children":"!"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Fun fact:"}]," ","Le plus grand toboggan de terrain de jeu permanent au monde mesure plus de 30 mètres — à peu près aussi haut qu'un immeuble de dix étages !"]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"margin":"20px 0 16px"},"children":null}],["$","p",null,{"className":"asset-note","children":"Printable PDF path is not present in the export JSON."}],"$L10",["$","$L11",null,{"title":"Aire de jeux de montagnes russes Dot-à-Dot Imprimable - PDF Gratuit","imageUrl":"","compact":true}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"0.8rem","color":"var(--muted)","marginTop":10,"lineHeight":1.5},"children":"No sign-up needed. Opens as a PDF. Print on US Letter (8.5 × 11 inch) or A4 paper. Free for home and classroom use."}],["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/fr/playgrounds/","style":{"display":"inline-flex","alignItems":"center","gap":6,"marginTop":18,"fontWeight":800,"color":"#d94f70","textDecoration":"none"},"children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":16,"height":16,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-left","aria-hidden":"true","children":[["$","path","1l729n",{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7"}],["$","path","x3x0zl",{"d":"M19 12H5"}],"$undefined"]}]," Back to all ","Playgrounds"," puzzles"]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"id":"dot-guide","className":"section","style":{"paddingTop":0,"maxWidth":800,"margin":"0 auto","padding":"0 24px 48px"},"children":[["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2rem)","marginBottom":12},"children":["Aire de jeux de montagnes russes"," Dot-to-Dot Puzzle Guide"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"color":"var(--muted)","lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":28},"dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"Six sections. Cent trente-trois points. C'est le plus grand puzzle de la série, et il ne s'en cache pas : le parcours monte, descend, fait des boucles, puis redescend jusqu'à son point de départ. Les enfants qui ont déjà terminé les grilles de balançoire, de toboggan ou de bascule reconnaîtront le format, mais la longueur de celui-ci change complètement la donne. La patience et la régularité sont la clé du succès. Trouvez le point 1 au pied de la première colline, et construisons ensemble un pu…"}}],[["$","div","1–20",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingLeft":16,"borderLeft":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["1–20"," — ","La colline de l'ascenseur"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Commencez au point 1 et poursuivez jusqu'au point 22 pour tracer la longue et abrupte montée qui propulse le wagonnet jusqu'à son point culminant. Ces lignes forment une diagonale régulière, ce qui permet de bien s'entraîner avant que le puzzle ne se complexifie."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"La plupart des montagnes russes utilisent un système de remontée par chaîne pour hisser le wagon en haut de la première montée ; c’est généralement la seule partie du parcours motorisée. Après le sommet, tout repose uniquement sur la gravité et l’inertie."]}]]}]]}],["$","div","21–40",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingLeft":16,"borderLeft":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["21–40"," — ","La première goutte"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Continuez du point 23 au point 44 pour suivre la descente abrupte depuis le sommet. L'angle y est plus prononcé qu'ailleurs sur la feuille ; privilégiez donc une main ferme et assurée plutôt qu'une main tremblante et hésitante : une descente rapide exige un trait rapide et sûr."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"La toute première descente d'un grand huit est presque toujours la plus haute et la plus abrupte de tout le parcours. Les concepteurs la placent intentionnellement au début, car c'est généralement là que le circuit atteint sa vitesse maximale."]}]]}]]}],["$","div","41–60",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingLeft":16,"borderLeft":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["41–60"," — ","La boucle"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Suivez les points 45 à 66 pour former la grande boucle au cœur du parcours. Cette section décrit une courbe sur elle-même, plus délicate qu'une montée ou une descente directe ; ralentissez et vérifiez le point suivant avant de vous engager dans chaque virage."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"Les premières montagnes russes à looping utilisaient une boucle parfaitement circulaire, et les passagers se plaignaient souvent de douleurs cervicales dues au changement brutal de force. Les loopings modernes utilisent une forme en goutte d'eau, beaucoup plus douce pour le corps à vitesse égale."]}]]}]]}],["$","div","61–85",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingLeft":16,"borderLeft":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["61–85"," — ","Les collines de Camelback"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Reliez les points 67 à 88 pour dessiner les petites collines qui suivent la boucle. Ces reliefs s'enchaînent rapidement, permettant aux enfants de s'exercer à des traits courts et précis plutôt qu'à de grands mouvements amples."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__icon","aria-hidden":"true","children":"💡"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guide-fact__body","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"guide-fact__label","children":"Fun fact!"}],["$","br",null,{}],"Ces petites montées sont parfois appelées « bosses de chameau » car leur succession ressemble aux bosses d'un chameau. Les cyclistes ressentent souvent un bref soulèvement de leur selle au sommet de chacune d'elles – un véritable, quoique court, instant d'apesanteur."]}]]}]]}],["$","div","86–102",{"style":{"marginBottom":24,"paddingLeft":16,"borderLeft":"3px solid var(--blue-light, #63b3ed)"},"children":[["$","h3",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"1rem","fontWeight":800,"marginBottom":6},"children":["86–102"," — ","Le dernier tour"]}],["$","p",null,{"style":{"lineHeight":1.7,"marginBottom":6},"children":"Travaillez du point 89 au point 110 pour dessiner la courbe ample qui ramène la voie vers la gare. Ce virage est large et progressif, un changement de rythme agréable après la boucle plus serrée du début du puzzle."}],["$","div",null,{"className":